From: HakiOS
Subject: [PATCH 0155] sweet wifi: PMEM_RPMH ioctl + typed RPMh lookup for BCM/ARC (0147 fix)

Rung 1 could not pass as built: 0147 shipped /dev/pmem without the
PMEM_RPMH ioctl (wland's first pm_rpmh() returned ENOTTY and exited), and
rh_lookup() accepted only VRM (slave 4) while BCM SN15/CN0 are slave 5 and
cx.lvl/mss.lvl are ARC slave 3.

bsd/dev/sweet_pmem.c: struct pmem_rpmh + PMEM_RPMH _IOW('P',5) (same
layout as phone/wifi/pmem.h); pm_ioctl handles it before taking
sweet_pmem_lock because it waits for an RPMh TCS; logs the result.

bsd/dev/sweet_rpmh.c:
- RH_ARC 3, RH_BCM 5; rh_lookup(res, expected_slave, &addr) checks the
  slave from the cmd-db header and the alignment (16 for VRM, 4 for
  ARC/BCM). Touch's ldoc11 path still uses RH_VRM: unchanged.
- sweet_rpmh_write() whitelists the WCN3990/modem supplies only:
  ldoa9 600-800, ldoc1 1600-2000, ldoc2 1200-1400, ldoc10 3100-3400 mV,
  plus the donor-tree variants ldoa1/ldoa7/ldoc11; rfclka2 enable;
  cx.lvl/mss.lvl index < 16. Everything else (touch L11C included) is
  refused with EPERM. It picks RH_ARC for the level resources and RH_VRM
  otherwise.
- sweet_rpmh_bcm_vote() looks up RH_BCM.

With this, the expected rung-1 lines are "BCM SN15 ... -> 0" and
"SWEET SMMU: BCM votes SN15=0 CN0=0".
